rows=[
 ('Q240','Rejected capture leaves graph edits pending while restoring only browsing memory','ports/graphshell/src/capture.rs:ingest_batch/forget_url; mere_host.rs:stage/prepare_store','source-confirmed consistency defect; full public native probe pending',
  'Both capture operations mutate MereHost immediately but clone/restore only self.memory when staging or outer apply fails. The local ledger and staged access-record writes are discarded, while MereHost changes remain pending. Later stage/persist writes all pending graph changes without recovering the discarded matching ledger/trace/authority records. Existing retry tests redeliver the identical event, which can mask this divergence. The prepared diagnostic instead uses a different successful delivery after refusal; it has not executed.',
  'Coordinate graph/session, encounter ledger, access records and browsing memory as one candidate installed after one acknowledged commit. Reuse the shared transaction lifecycle rather than invent another graph rollback or using undo to hide rejected work. This is a larger consistency seam to document, not a production patch in this audit.'),
 ('Q241','History-only forgetting retracts traversal assertions without capture ownership','ports/graphshell/src/capture.rs:forget_browser_history','source-confirmed ownership mismatch; public native counterexample pending',
  'HistoryOnly preserves the node but enumerates every incident RelationKind::Traversal and issues RetractRelations with the whole Traversal family. Neither the collecting filter nor retraction selects browser encounter/source/author ownership. Traversal assertions created by other applications are therefore included. The prepared public diagnostic supplies one other-application incident traversal and an unrelated-pair control; it has not executed.',
  'Retract the exact capture-owned assertion handles and remove derived capture evidence without clearing another application\'s traversal family. Preserve shared source identity and other authors\' assertions; choosing a coarser privacy-erasure policy would require an explicit contract change.'),
 ('Q242','Browser capture ignores the configured trace segment size','ports/graphshell/src/capture.rs:ingest_batch/HistoryCapturePolicy','source-confirmed unused policy; public native comparison pending',
  'The configured segment_size is passed into BrowsingMemory, but ingest_batch ignores every record_traversal flush-threshold result and flushes only at the end. One owner\'s delivery becomes one segment regardless of the configured threshold. set_policy also replaces only the policy field. The prepared native check compares size1 and64 on three events; it has not executed.',
  'Honor the existing segment threshold inside the staged outer batch, while keeping one durable delivery commit. Qualify retention/quota and replay behavior rather than splitting the durable transaction per event or keeping a visible setting that has no effect.'),
 ('Q243','Extension configuration races the serialized queue and can lose visits or restore excluded URLs','ports/graphshell/web/extension/background.js:handleMessage capture.configure/queueVisits','actual complete source reproduced in native Node VM',
  'queueVisits and ack use serializedQueueMutation; capture.configure reads and writes the same queue outside it. An explicitly delayed configure snapshot overwrites a newly queued visit with an empty queue. Reversing the delayed write lets queueVisits restore a URL after a completed configuration excluded that origin. A sequential configuration control preserves eligible visits and removes excluded ones.',
  'Route every queue/policy read-modify-write through the same serialization owner and check the effective policy at that transition. Include configuration and permission-removal writes rather than layering a second queue guard.'),
 ('Q244','Extension queue silently suppresses exact source-fact conflicts the ledger rejects','ports/graphshell/web/extension/capture-model.js:mergeQueue; crates/eidetic/eidetic-core/src/import/encounters.rs:same_source_facts','paired actual Node and public Rust counterexamples reproduced',
  'For the same scoped identity and millisecond time, changing original_unix_micros or source_is_local is silently replaced by the prior queue entry. The actual Rust ledger rejects both changes as conflicting source facts. Exact duplicate delivery and a visible URL-conflict refusal are controls. Preserving the earlier value hides the conflicting observation before the owner can inspect or refuse it.',
  'Share the immutable source-fact contract across queue and ledger adapters. Keep mutable title/acquisition attribution distinctions explicit, while retaining or refusing exact time/locality conflicts instead of silently deduplicating them.'),
 ('Q245','JavaScript resource assembly bypasses both integrity checks implemented by the shared Rust owner','ports/graphshell/web/extension/resource-chunk.js:ResourceAssembly.accept; crates/chirograph/src/lib.rs:ResourceAssembly/ResourceChunkResponse::decode','paired actual JavaScript and shared Rust assembler counterexamples reproduced',
  'Complete JavaScript assembly accepts altered payload bytes under an unchanged chunk hash, and also accepts a correctly chunk-addressed altered payload under a different whole-resource hash. The same exact synthetic BLAKE3 fixtures are rejected by the actual shared Rust assembler as CorruptChunk and WrongResource. Valid-frame and wrong-session controls retain the expected distinctions. validateHash checks only the shape of a hash array.',
  'Adopt shared verified resource assembly at the browser boundary, or supply an explicit equivalent digest contract for both chunk and final resource. Preserve session, order, length and bounded acquisition checks; metadata equality does not verify bytes.'),
 ('Q246','POSIX extension preparation omits the bounded action-form module loaded by its bridge','ports/graphshell/web/extension/prepare-extension.sh; bridge.html; bridge.js','source-confirmed packaging defect; installer/browser package not executed',
  'bridge.html loads action-form.js, resource-chunk.js and bridge.js. PowerShell copies all three; the POSIX preparation script copies only the latter two. In a clean destination GraphshellActionForm is unavailable and renderBoundedActionForm returns false, leaving ordinary bounded actions such as transfer acceptance unrendered. An old destination file can mask the omission. The receipt is a source dependency check, not an executed package/browser trial.',
  'Keep one required package-file inventory across shell and PowerShell preparations, and verify a clean prepared package includes every declared script dependency. Do not rely on stale destination files to supply an omitted module.'),
]
